# ==============================================================================
#  JS8MapChat — .gitignore
#  Lives at:  C:\Users\KW3KW\Documents\Claude AI\JS8MapChat\.gitignore
#  Created 2026-07-14 (ticket #8 — first version control in this project)
#
#  RULE OF THUMB: git tracks SOURCE. It does not track builds, runtime state,
#  data, or backups. If you can rebuild it or the app rewrites it, it goes here.
# ==============================================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. THE BACKUP TREES.  THE MOST IMPORTANT LINES IN THIS FILE.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  "Backup Version\" holds a FULL second copy of the FastChat tree (under
#  July 7th\). See H1b in the architecture doc.  If it enters the repo, every
#  source file exists TWICE in history, every grep goes ambiguous, and the
#  ghost-copy problem is preserved forever in version control.
#
#  THE FOLDER STAYS ON DISK. It is the operator's scratch backup. Git just
#  never looks at it.  (Once git is trusted, this folder becomes redundant —
#  that is the POINT of #8. Retire it when you're ready, not before.)

Backup Version/
BACKUP VERSIONS/


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  2. BUILD OUTPUT — rebuildable, and huge
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  A onefile PyInstaller exe is tens of MB. One per commit will bloat this
#  repo fast, and the exe is NOT the truth — the source + the .spec is.
#  Build_JS8FastChat.bat wipes build\ and dist\ every run anyway.

build/
dist/
installer_output/
*.exe
*.msi

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3. THE SHARED MAILBOX — runtime state, not source
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  These six JSON files are written and deleted by the running apps, constantly.
#  Committing them would mean a diff on every single launch.
#  THE CONTRACT (who writes what) lives in the architecture doc §3 — that IS
#  tracked. The files themselves are not.

JS8MapChat Shared/
js8fastchat_intent.json
js8map_raise_fastchat.json
js8map_server.json
js8map_outgoing_tx.json
js8map_tx_lease.json
js8fastchat_alive.json


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  4. PER-USER APP STATE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Post-#26 the LIVE copies of these live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\JS8MapChat\FastChat\
#  (outside the repo entirely — good). The copies still sitting beside the code
#  are DECOYS: nothing reads them. Do not track a decoy.

mjs_js8fastchat_3_2_config.json
mjs_js8maps_3_0_config.json
js8fastchat_layout_3_2.json
js8fastchat_tx_history_3_3.json
js8fastchat_capture_3_4.json
ham_map_config.json
map_window_profile/


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  5. LOGS AND DATABASES — data, not code
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*.log
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  6. ROLLBACK COPIES
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  constants_BACKUP_pre26.py.bak, JS8Map_BACKUP_pre_42patch.py.bak, etc.
#  These exist BECAUSE there was no git. They are the thing git replaces.
#  Keep them on disk for now (they are a working rollback). Don't track them —
#  a tracked .bak is just a confusing duplicate of a file git already has.

*.bak
*.tmp
*.orig
*~


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  7. WINDOWS / EDITOR NOISE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
Desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/


# ==============================================================================
#  DELIBERATELY **TRACKED** — do not add these to the list above
# ==============================================================================
#   JS8Map.py, JS8FastChat_Ver_3_5_7.py, js8fastchat\**\*.py   the source
#   *.spec                     the build recipes — the exe is reproducible ONLY
#                              from these. Losing a .spec loses the build.
#   *.bat, *.vbs               the launchers. The VBS is the script-mode
#                              fallback (§6). It is SOURCE. Never delete it.
#   *.iss                      JS8Map.iss — the installer script.
#   index.html, app.js, app.css, boot.js      the browser map UI
#   *.ico, *.png               icons and bundled assets (small; the .spec ships
#                              them; a lost icon means a wrong-icon exe — §13 #6)
#   CHANGELOG.txt, BUILD_NOTES.txt, *.md      the durable docs
#   js8_groups.json            user-assigned group colours — small, and the app
#                              reads it. TRACKED ON PURPOSE, but see note below.
#
#  ⚠ UNPROVEN — decide these consciously, do not let them drift in:
#   ham_map.html      generated at runtime? or a template the app copies out?
#                     If GENERATED, add it above. NOT CHECKED. Look before you
#                     commit a file the app rewrites on every launch.
#   js8_groups.json   user data that happens to live beside the source. Tracked
#                     for now because it is small and losing it loses his groups.
#                     If it churns on every run, move it out.
# ==============================================================================
Zip Files/
JS8Map Ver 1.75/boot.js
js8_spots.db-shm
js8_spots.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Scratch for this refactor - not part of the source tree
/preflight_snapshot.json

# user-assigned group colours -- churns on every sync/prune, holds the
# operator's own groups. Untracked per the "move it out" note below.
JS8Map Ver 1.75/js8_groups.json

# Linux package output - 15 MB, rebuilt any time by make_js8map_package.sh
*.tar.gz
 
